docs {
  # Create Booking
  Creates a new booking for a specific time slot. This is a public endpoint that doesn't require authentication.
  
  ## Request Body
  ```json
  {
    "guest_name": string,  // Name of the guest
    "guest_email": string, // Email of the guest
    "date": string,       // YYYY-MM-DD format
    "time": string        // HH:mm format (appointment start time)
  }
  ```
  
  ## Response
  ```json
  {
    "item": {
      "id": number,
      "provider_id": number,    // ID of the service provider
      "guest_id": number,       // ID of the guest/client
      "guest_name": string,     // Name of the guest
      "guest_email": string,    // Email of the guest
      "date": string,          // YYYY-MM-DD format
      "start_time": string,    // RFC3339 format
      "end_time": string,      // RFC3339 format
      "status": string,        // pending, confirmed, cancelled, completed
      "created_at": string,    // RFC3339 format
      "updated_at": string     // RFC3339 format
    },
    "message": "Booking created successfully"
  }
  ```
  
  ## Notes
  - Validates availability before creating booking
  - Handles timezone conversions
  - Prevents double bookings
  - Sends confirmation email (if configured)
  
  ## Errors
  - 400: Invalid input data
  - 404: Provider not found
  - 409: Time slot not available
  - 500: Server error
}
